# Round 18, C1-12 (follows). L §5.3: "rows of one target in one version are ordered by precedence (§4.6 step 3), and
# two it leaves tied are refused (LOAD-OVERLAP, step 4)". x[a] = 5 (the version's always) and x[a] = 7 governs 2027..
# in one version: the row with a span beats the one with always (§4.6 step 3.3), so 5 in 2026 and 7 in 2027.
=== m.tally
model m
  tally 2
  on 2027-12-31
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31
source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index ks = [a, b]
input x[k in ks]: money PLN
def r[k in ks, d in days]: money PLN = x[k] at d
version v1
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  x[a] = 5
  x[a] = 7 governs 2027..
  x[b] = 1
ask q: r[a, 2026-06-01], r[a, 2027-06-01], r[b, 2027-06-01]
=== expect
q: (5.00 PLN, 7.00 PLN, 1.00 PLN)
  cut 2027-12-31
